<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-Tetra Tech estimates raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Tetra Tech estimates raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gruntal &amp; Co raised its profit estimates for 1997 and 1998 for Tetra Tech Inc after the company said it agreed to buy Whalen &amp; Co.</p>
<p>-- Analyst Jeffrey Robins said in a report that the acquisition moves the company into the market for engineering and management services for the wireless telecommunications market, which could be a major new source of growth over the next several years.</p>
<p>-- He raised fiscal year to September 1997 EPS to $0.90 from $0.88 and year to September 1998 EPS to $1.15 from $1.10. Maintains strong buy and 12-month price target of $30.</p>
<p>-- Shares rose 1-1/8 to 18-5/8.</p>
</text>
